==Latvian==
{{slim-wikipedia|lang=lv}}
[[File:Lager_beer_in_glass.jpg|thumb|200px|Alus]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|lv|bat-pro|*alu-}}, from {{inh|lv|ine-pro|*h₂elut-||bitter}}. A minority view considers the Latvian and Lithuanian terms to be ultimately [[borrowing]]s from {{cog|gem}}, via {{cog|prg|-}}. Cognates include {{cog|lt|alùs}}, {{cog|prg|alu||honey drink}}, {{cog|orv|олъ||strong drink}}, {{cog|bg|оловина||beer yeast|tr=olovína}}, {{cog|sl|ol|ôl|beer}}, {{cog|ang|ealu}}, {{m|ang|alu}}, {{cog|en|ale}}, {{cog|non|ǫl||beer; feast}}, {{cog|grc|ἀλύδοιμος||bitter}}.<ref>{{R:lv:LEV}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{lv-IPA|alus}}
{{audio|lv-riga-alus.ogg|lang=lv}}

===Noun===
{{lv-noun|m|3rd}}

# [[beer]] {{gloss|[[alcoholic]] [[beverage]] [[usually]] [[make|made]] with [[barley]] [[malt]] and [[hop]]s}}
#: {{ux|lv|gaišais '''alus'''|lager (lit. light '''beer''')|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|tumšais '''alus'''|dark '''beer'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|mājas '''alus'''|home '''beer'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|amatnieku '''alus'''|craft '''beer'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|med'''alus'''|honey '''beer'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|'''alus''' muca|'''beer''' barrel, keg|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|'''alus''' kauss|'''beer''' mug|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|'''alus''' darītava|brewery (lit. '''beer''' making place)|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|'''alus''' rūpniecība|'''beer''' industry|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|darīt, vārīt '''alu'''|to make (lit. to do), to brew (lit. to boil) '''beer'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|Jāņiem tika brūvēts '''alus''', un nu staigāja no mutes uz muti liela, zaļa māla krūze, putām pārsegta, rūgteni smaržīga dzēriena pilna|in midsummer '''beer''' was brewed, and then a big, green clay jug went from mouth to mouth, covered with foam and full of (that) bitter, aromatic drink|inline=1}}

